clean_summary:
SWE-Bench isimli yeni benchmark, modellerin internet olmadan sıfırdan gerçek yürütülebilir programları (ffmpeg, SQLite, ripgrep) yeniden oluşturup oluşturamayacağını sorguluyor. 9 önde gelen LLM, sıfır çekmiş.

LLM’lerin eğitim verilerinde yer almadığını bildiğimiz yeni benchmarklardaki performanslarının düşüklüğü hiç şaşırtıcı değil. Çünkü bu modeller eğitim verileri kadar bilgiye sahipler ve yeni bir şey öğrenmeleri için baştan eğitilmeleri gerekiyor.

@deedydas: "The creators of SWE-Bench just dropped a really simple new benchmark every LLM gets 0% on. ProgramBench asks: can models recreate real executable programs (ffmpeg, SQLite, ripgrep) from scratch with no internet? We are far from saturated on model quality."

We’re basically using dropout on the AI development community. On this pass of model development, you have to figure out how to get the right answer without that neuron (the internet) that you’ve been over-relying on. We’ll let you use it at test-time when you’re deployed, but trust me that you’ll be a better model if I force you to compensate with other means during training and development. And it’s actually true.

Nice work @jyangballin and co! Eval legends.

@jyangballin: "How much of SQLite, FFmpeg, PHP compiler can LMs code from scratch? Given just an executable and no starter code or internet access. Introducing ProgramBench: 200 rigorous, whole-repo generation tasks where models design, build, and ship a working program end to end."

